    "body": "Part of #36692.\n\n- `descriptor_tests`: `DoCheck` built the spending transaction with `vin.resize(1)` / `vout.resize(1)` and then wrote `nSequence` through `vin[0]`. It now uses literal `vin`/`vout` lists, which also makes the default input and the empty output visible.\n- `bip352_tests`: `bip352_p2pkh_pubkey_extraction_with_checksig_in_scriptsig` signed a transaction and then wrote the malleated scriptSig into its existing input. It is now split into an unsigned transaction used for signing and the final transaction built with the malleated scriptSig. The legacy sighash replaces the scriptSig being signed with the scriptCode, so the signature does not depend on the scriptSig.\n- `group_outputs_tests`: the `addCoin` helper used `vout.resize(1)` followed by writes to `nValue` and `scriptPubKey`. It now uses a literal `vout` list.\n- `bench/mempool_ephemeral_spends`: `tx2` was built with `vin.resize()` followed by writes to each input's `prevout`. Its inputs are now constructed from their outpoints, and the single default input of `tx1` and the single empty output of `tx2` are literal lists. The transactions are unchanged.\n\nNo change in test or benchmark behavior.\n",
